The Quillbrook Public Library Board (the Owner) invites stipulated price tenders from electrical contractors for the electrical fit-out of the main floor of the library building at 2150 Heron Crescent, Quillbrook, Alberta. The Owner's consultant for this work is Brightline Consulting Engineers Ltd.

= 1. Scope of work

Supply and install the new electrical distribution, lighting, and wiring devices for the main floor fit-out, as shown on drawings E-000 to E-102 and specified in Division 26. The work includes:

- a new feeder from a spare breaker in the existing main distribution panel to a new 75 kVA dry-type transformer;
- a new 225 A, 42-circuit panelboard LP-1 fed from the transformer;
- LED troffer lighting, exit signs, and emergency battery units, with local switching;
- duplex receptacles throughout the fit-out area;
- branch circuit wiring in EMT, testing, and a typed panel directory.

Fire alarm, data, and security systems are by others and are not part of this tender. The base building shell is complete and there is no demolition.

= 2. Tender documents

The tender documents are this invitation, the Division 26 specification issued with it, and the following drawings, all revision 0, issued for tender on 2026-09-08. The specification is a separate document, `division-26-specification.pdf`.

