= 3. Submission

The closing date and time for tenders will be issued by addendum.

Address the tender to: Quillbrook Public Library Board, Attention: Dana Whitfield, Facilities Coordinator, 2150 Heron Crescent, Quillbrook, Alberta. Submit one PDF by email to tenders\@quillbrooklibrary.example with the tender number in the subject line.

= 4. Form of tender

Tender a stipulated lump sum price in Canadian dollars for the whole of the work, excluding GST. A schedule of values is not required at tender stage; the successful contractor provides one before the first progress claim. The tender is a written proposal that states the lump sum price, the scope included, and the tenderer's assumptions and exclusions.

= 5. Site visit

An optional site visit is held at 10:00 a.m. on Tuesday, 6 October 2026, at the library's main entry. Attendance is not mandatory.

= 6. Questions

Send questions by email to tenders\@quillbrooklibrary.example. Answers are issued to all tenderers by addendum.

= 7. Alternates and unit prices

No alternates or unit prices are requested.

= 8. Bid security

The Owner has not yet confirmed the bid security requirement for this tender. Tenderers must confirm with the Owner's contact whether bid security is required, and in what form, before submitting a tender. A tender submitted without confirming the bid security requirement is non-compliant and will be rejected.

= 9. Insurance

The successful contractor carries commercial general liability insurance of not less than \$5,000,000 per occurrence, naming the Owner as an additional insured, for the duration of the work.

= 10. Schedule and working hours

The work is to be complete within eight weeks of award. Work inside the library is permitted between 7:00 a.m. and 5:00 p.m., Monday to Friday. The connection at the existing main distribution panel requires a shutdown outside library opening hours, coordinated with the Owner.

= 11. Contract

The contract is CCDC 2, stipulated price contract, with the Owner's supplementary conditions. The Owner may accept any tender or reject all tenders.
